\subsubsection{The staging area}

The fourth item tests what [[git add]] does: it stages an existing change for
the next commit, moving it from the working tree into the index
(\cref{sec:staging}).
Two distractors are documented misconceptions: that [[git add file]] creates a
file rather than staging it \autocite[Sec.~5.3]{IsomottonenCochez2014}, and
the add-as-commit reading that it already records the version.

