\subsubsection{Remotes and collaboration}

The ninth item tests that push moves your local commits to another copy of the
repository---there is no single cloud original, only copies by convention
(\cref{sec:remotes}).
The key distractor is push-as-save-to-cloud: saving files to the one true copy
on a server, the main-copy thinking that the basic-workflow misconception
catalogue targets \autocite{Postner2026GitMisconceptions}.

